le out obstructive biliary disease as the primary diagnosis?", "summary": "Absence of jaundice and clay-colored stools moderately argues against obstructive biliary disease as the primary diagnosis, though RUQ pain with shock could still reflect an atypical presentation."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of jaundice and presence of acne/weight loss argue against alcohol-induced pancreatitis despite high daily consumption?", "summary": "Absence of jaundice and presence of acne/weight loss moderately argue against alcohol-induced pancreatitis, though heavy alcohol use alone could still contribute to this diagnosis."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B1", 0.452], ["B2", 0.323], ["B3", 0.172]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.385], ["B2", 0.33], ["B4", 0.176]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": true, "reason": "The patient exhibits hypotension (80/40 mmHg) and tachycardia (110 bpm) consistent with shock, along with severe localized right upper quadrant pain (10/10 tenderness) suggesting acute abdomen. These findings meet universal instability criteria for haemodynamic instability and require immediate stabilization before diagnostic resolution.", "required_actions": ["Administer intravenous fluids (confirm adequacy of current bolus)", "Order CBC, coagulation panel, and type/crossmatch for potential transfusion", "Prepare for emergent surgical evaluation for possible ruptured ectopic pregnancy or acute intra-abdominal hemorrhage"]}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading branch posterior (0.385) < 0.75 threshold, dangerous alternatives (B1: 0.9 danger, B2: 0.8 danger) remain unresolved, and emergency override requires stabilization before diagnostic refinement. Tree depth (1) < max allowed depth (3)."}, "turn_budget_used": 2, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.55, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.38461538461538464, "benchmar