entials, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology, abnormal circulating copper concentration, abnormal cranial nerve morphology\n  Favours second: abnormality of the face, agenesis of lateral incisor, bilateral cleft lip, bilateral cleft palate, bulbous nose\n\nBiliary Obstruction with Acute Presentation vs Acute Pancreatic Inflammation:\n  Favours first:  clay-colored stools, dark urine, fatigue, fever, jaundice\n  Favours second: abnormality of the face, agenesis of lateral incisor, autosomal dominant inheritance, bilateral cleft lip, bilateral cleft palate\n\nRelated to Hepatic Vascular Occlusion: budd-chiari syndrome, hepatic infarction, hepatic vein thrombosis\n\nRelated to Acute Pancreatic Inflammation: disease of orbital part of eye adnexa, orbital cellulitis, orbital osteomyelitis\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  A 23-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with severe abdominal pain → pain → Hepatic Vascular Occlusion\n  A 23-year-old woman presents to the emergency department with severe abdominal pain → shoulder pain → Hepatic Vascular Occlusion\n  The pain has been dull and progressive → pain → Hepatic Vascular Occlusion"}
